  |  REGION A    |        REGION B          |       REGION C         |
  |              |                          |                        |
  | Track FAILS  | Track OK                 | Track OK               |
  | Trace FAILS  | Trace FAILS              | Trace OK               |
  |              |                          |                        |
  | REFUSAL      | ENVELOPE REQUIRED        | GROUND AUTHORISATION   |
  | (no envelope)| or REFUSAL               | VIABLE (delegation     |
  |              |                          |  still permitted)      |
  |              |                          |                        |

  lambda*_track = -lambda_g / ln(tau_T)     ~ 0.0513 * lambda_g  at tau_T = 0.95
  lambda*_halt  = rho_h

  JOINT frontier lambda* (all three constraints) = lambda*_halt absent an
  envelope; envelope specificity can lower it toward lambda*_track.
```

Reading: three regions, derived from Theorem 1(i)–(iii). Region B is the analytically interesting one: ground control can still track the operator's reasons but cannot halt before commitment, so tracing fails while tracking holds. Two honest caveats: (a) the envelope exception in Theorem 1(iii) rescues tracing, and whether an envelope can also rescue tracking in Region A is not established — it would require the envelope to encode tracking reasons in advance, and the framework flags this as open; (b) the ordering $\lambda^*_{track} < \lambda^*_{halt}$ holds because $\lambda_g = 2\delta + \rho_h \geq \rho_h$, so $0.0513\lambda_g < \rho_h$ for any $\delta < 9.25\rho_h$ — effectively always, but the figure should be read as conditional on that.

